body:
## Summary

In the Agents/Sessions window (Copilot CLI agent host chat), a response can finish streaming and be **fully and correctly written into the DOM**, yet remain **visually stale/clipped** — the chat list simply never grows to show the tail of the response — until something forces the virtualized list to fully re-layout (e.g. shrinking the window and then maximizing it again). Once that forced relayout happens, the already-rendered content appears immediately, with no further backend activity.

This reproduced on my machine on the order of 9/10 times when a response finishes with a large final content update.

## Root cause

`fireItemHeightChange()` in [`src/vs/workbench/contrib/chat/browser/widget/chatListRenderer.ts`](https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/blob/bca199a6ffc2092a325e9bc1f32b56734a554dc5/src/vs/workbench/contrib/chat/browser/widget/chatListRenderer.ts#L525-L564) (lines 525-564):

```ts
private fireItemHeightChange(template: IChatListItemTemplate, measuredHeight?: number): void {
    if (!template.currentElement || !template.rowContainer.isConnected) {
        return;
    }

    const height = measuredHeight ?? template.rowContainer.getBoundingClientRect().height;
    if (height === 0 || !height) {
        return;
    }

    const normalizedHeight = Math.ceil(height);
    if (normalizedHeight === template.currentElement.currentRenderedHeight) {
        return;
    }

    const originalStoredHeight = template.currentElement.currentRenderedHeight;
    template.currentElement.currentRenderedHeight = normalizedHeight;
    if (template.currentElement === this._elementBeingRendered) {
        return;
    }

    if (typeof originalStoredHeight === 'number') {
        this._onDidChangeItemHeight.fire({ element: template.currentElement, height: normalizedHeight });
    } else {
        // ...deferred first-measurement branch...
    }
}
```

`_elementBeingRendered` is set for the full duration of `renderElement()`'s synchronous call ([lines 909-916](https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/blob/bca199a6ffc2092a325e9bc1f32b56734a554dc5/src/vs/workbench/contrib/chat/browser/widget/chatListRenderer.ts#L909-L916)).

The failure sequence:

1. A response transitions to `isComplete` and does its final, non-progressive render (`renderChatResponseBasic`), which can add a large chunk of content in one synchronous pass (in the incident I traced, a ~160-word catch-up burst landed in the same tick that a trailing tool-call/working-progress indicator was torn down).
2. Something reports the new (larger) height **synchronously**, mid-render — e.g. a markdown/code-block part's `onDidChangeHeight` (wired at [line 3651](https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/blob/bca199a6ffc2092a325e9bc1f32b56734a554dc5/src/vs/workbench/contrib/chat/browser/widget/chatListRenderer.ts#L3651)), or a working-progress part finalizing. Because this happens while `_elementBeingRendered === template.currentElement`, `fireItemHeightChange` **commits** the correct new height into `template.currentElement.currentRenderedHeight` but **returns without notifying** (`_onDidChangeItemHeight` never fires).
3. Shortly after, the row's real DOM `ResizeObserver` ([lines 870-876](https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/blob/bca199a6ffc2092a325e9bc1f32b56734a554dc5/src/vs/workbench/contrib/chat/browser/widget/chatListRenderer.ts#L870-L876)) fires asynchronously, reporting that same final height. But now the *first* guard (`normalizedHeight === template.currentElement.currentRenderedHeight`) short-circuits it too, because step 2 already silently recorded that exact value.
4. Net effect: `_onDidChangeItemHeight` **never fires** for the row's true final height, so the owning `ChatListWidget` never calls `tree.updateElementHeight()`. The virtualized list keeps using the stale, smaller, mid-stream row height to position/clip content — even though the DOM itself already contains the full, correct response. A window resize forces a full list re-layout (and recycles the row out of/back into the viewport), which re-measures from scratch and reveals the already-rendered content.

## Why this is intermittent, not 100%

Whether the notification gets swallowed depends on whether a height-affecting callback happens to fire **synchronously inside** the same call stack as the final completion render (as opposed to only being reported later, purely via the async `ResizeObserver`, in which case there's no bug). That depends on the shape of the response (code blocks, tool-call/working-indicator teardown timing) and JS microtask/callback ordering, which varies turn to turn.

## Likely regression source

This double-guard shape was introduced by commit [`725d69a9a85b`](https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/commit/725d69a9a85b62e7a9fae7faf6de52207d85f0ac) ("fix cutoff chat requests", #318385) — which, ironically, added the `_elementBeingRendered` reentrancy guard to fix a *different* clipping issue, but in doing so introduced this new swallow path.

## Suggested fix direction

Don't commit the new height to `currentRenderedHeight` until it's known the notification can actually be delivered; when hit mid-render, defer the whole measure-and-notify step (re-invoking `fireItemHeightChange` itself) until after the render pass completes, e.g. via the same `dom.scheduleAtNextAnimationFrame` pattern already used elsewhere in this method for first-measurement scheduling, instead of silently dropping the update.

## Evidence

Diagnosed from an exported Agent Host log bundle (Agent Host.log, Window.log, Shared.log, AHP protocol log, SDK events.jsonl) for an incident session:
- The AHP protocol log showed the backend delivered the final turn's `chat/delta`/`chat/turnComplete` actions cleanly with no dropped/out-of-order `serverSeq`.
- `Window.log` traces confirmed `ChatListItemRenderer` actually completed writing the full final response into the DOM within ~40ms of turn completion (ruling out a "message never arrived" bug).
- The progressive-render timer showed a ~3s dead zone with zero ticks, then a rapid multi-hundred-word catch-up burst landing on the same tick as the completion flush — consistent with the trigger condition described above.

## Verification status

A repro test targeting `fireItemHeightChange`'s guard logic directly is in progress; will update/link once landed.
